bejoin_mipsentry.elf -- MIPS32 big-endian hand-assembled image for option
bejoin callers with a proven pair whose second register one path leaves as it
came in (GH-904; tests/stages/kuna-bejoin-mipsclang.xml).

What it is
  Static executable from bejoin_mipsentry.s. sum_both computes $3 on both
  paths and reads it there for $2's carry; sum_or_entry does the same on one
  path and leaves $3 holding its entry value on the other. c_sum_both and
  c_sum_or_entry store both words of the result, which proves both 64-bit
  under option bejoin callers.

Why it is vendored
  CI has no MIPS toolchain, and no compiler emits sum_or_entry's shape on
  purpose.

Where it came from
  Ubuntu binutils 2.38 (mipsel-linux-gnu-as/-ld, -EB) on the host:

      mipsel-linux-gnu-as -EB -mips32 bejoin_mipsentry.s -o bejoin_mipsentry.o
      mipsel-linux-gnu-ld -EB -static --build-id=none -e __start \
          bejoin_mipsentry.o -o bejoin_mipsentry.elf

  sha256:
    a24cc47a5ad5a27a25fabee59c4387d53041674c10695bb753c8907949104abe  bejoin_mipsentry.elf
  Never executed.
